message: "If you use INOOR, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "INOOR: Iranian National Observatory Optical Reduction"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-02
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23879448
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/hosseintd/INOOR"
abstract: >-
  Here, we present the Iranian National Observatory Optical Reduction (INOOR)
  software package, a Python-based pipeline with a graphical user interface (GUI)
  designed for the data reduction and analysis of imaging observations obtained
  with the 3.4-meter telescope of the Iranian National Observatory (INO340). INOOR
  builds master calibration frames, calibrates and cleans the science frames, solves
  the astrometry, and performs aperture photometry on single frames and long time
  series, producing light curves and atmospheric extinction coefficients. Designed
  for transient follow-up, when complete calibration sets are often unavailable, it
  can construct an auto-flat directly from the science frames and remove cosmic
  rays and hot pixels in post-processing. Apertures can be set by FWHM scaling,
  signal-to-noise optimization, or the curve of growth, adapting to varying seeing
  and other changes in the PSF. INOOR is a step toward a more automated pipeline
  for the rapid follow-up of transients in the era of the Vera C. Rubin Observatory.
keywords:
  - astronomy software
  - data reduction
  - calibration
  - photometry
  - light curves
  - astrometry
  - INO340
